# =============================================================================
# CRM Leads — environment
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# Every variable below is read exactly once, in a validated module. A missing or
# malformed value fails at boot, never at 11am on a Tuesday.
# =============================================================================

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO roles, in EVERY environment including this one. Development connecting as
# the owner is what let the silo depend on a connection string for eight sprint
# items before a canary fixture caught it — a superuser or a schema owner reads
# straight through row level security, FORCE included, with no error anywhere.
#
#   crm_app      — what the running processes connect as. This is DATABASE_URL.
#   crm_migrator — owns the schema. Used ONLY by drizzle-kit and the seed.
#                  It is never present in an app process.
#
# The app REFUSES TO BOOT if DATABASE_URL names a role that can bypass RLS —
# see app/db/boot-assert.ts, Sprint-0 gate G4(a).
#
# The crm_app password is set out of band, never in a migration: `npm run
# db:seed` sets it locally, and the provider's console sets it in production.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://crm_app:crm_app_dev_only@localhost:5432/crm_dev
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://crm:crm@localhost:5432/crm_dev

# --- Process topology ---------------------------------------------------------
# The three processes are ONE image. This variable is the entire fold/split
# mechanism (ADR-01 / ADR-S1). Rung 1 (pilot) runs all three folded; rung 2
# splits them. Separating later requires no redesign and no migration.
#   web    — SSR, the resource API, the SSE hub
#   worker — pg-boss: reminders, health probe, sweepers, the outbox relay
#   ingest — /webhooks/* and /intake/* only. This is the bulkhead.
#
# WITH "worker" IN THIS LIST, THE WEB PROCESS RUNS THE DISPATCHER IN-PROCESS and
# REFUSES TO BOOT (JOBS002) when pg-boss has no schema. So `npm run db:jobs` is a
# prerequisite of `npm run dev`, not an optional extra.
#
# That refusal is deliberate and it is the same posture as the G4(a) assertion
# above: a web process that serves every page while silently firing none of its
# reminders looks healthy from every angle, and in a FOLDED topology there is no
# separate worker whose absence anyone would notice. A reminder is a legal
# artifact — it fires once, at the right moment, inside the legal calling window.
#
# To run a web process with no worker, drop it from the list: PROCESS_ROLES=web,ingest
#
# Unset defaults to ON, on purpose: a deployment that forgets this variable should
# run the reminders rather than silently not run them.
PROCESS_ROLES=web,worker,ingest

# --- Application --------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-in-every-environment

# --- Aloware (Sprint 0 spike) -------------------------------------------------
# No value here is verified yet. **Gate G2** of the §9 ladder establishes whether
# webhooks are signed, whether they retry, and with what vocabulary.
#
# ⚠️ This block used to say "Gate 11", which is the bundle and first-paint gate
# and has been closed since 2026-08-03. Older sections of the corpus also call
# this spike "Puerta 7" — that is the pre-merge numbering from thesis.md. §9
# consolidated both ladders and Aloware is G2 there. Reading the old number is
# how somebody concludes this gate is already closed.
#
# ALOWARE_WEBHOOK_SECRET is deliberately still commented out: whether Aloware
# signs its webhooks AT ALL is one of the things G2 measures. A variable that
# exists before the answer does invites a verification path built on a scheme
# nobody confirmed.
# ALOWARE_API_BASE=
# ALOWARE_API_TOKEN=
# ALOWARE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Sprint-0 G2 spike instruments --------------------------------------------
# The receiver's control plane can make the webhook endpoint return 500 or hang,
# which is how the retry and synchronous-response measurements are taken. On a
# public URL that is not a debug toggle — it decides what the gate observes — so
# the process REFUSES TO START without a secret of at least 16 characters.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# SPIKE_CONTROL_SECRET=
# SPIKE_EVIDENCE_DIR=evidence/aloware
#
# The dial/SMS subject, in E.164. It lives here and NEVER in the committed
# probe declaration: a subject is a real person, a declaration is permanent,
# and a git history is a longer clock than the one E9 forbids for PII.
# `[DESTINATION_E164]` in scripts/spike/aloware-probes.json resolves from this
# — the prober substitutes any `[NAME]` from `SPIKE_NAME`. A missing value is
# refused by SPIKE014 rather than sent as the literal placeholder.
# SPIKE_DESTINATION_E164=

# SMS_ENABLED IS NOT AN ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE. It is a column on `tenant`, and
# §10.16 bans `process.env.SMS*` anywhere in the tree — the flag is reachable
# only through app.compliance_check(). It lived here as a leftover from an
# earlier draft, which is exactly the kind of stale line someone implements
# from. The launch posture is still SMS-dark; the switch is a row, not a deploy.

# --- Observability ------------------------------------------------------------
# SENTRY_DSN=
# AXIOM_TOKEN=
